WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
September 2021. Natural gas
prices had nearly quadrupled since

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.850
the start of the year.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.390
A fertiliser firm halted
its two UK plants.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:15.190
Soon, poultry processors and drinks
makers were warning of disruption.

5
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.090
The government paid to restart one plant.

6
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.070
What could fertiliser possibly
have to do with fizzy drinks?

7
00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.180
And how can a change in one market move

8
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.770
prices in a completely different one?

9
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.760
In this mission, you'll meet
the ways goods are linked,

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.270
through buyers and through production.

11
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.710
Then you'll push up the price of one good,

12
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.110
and watch a second market react.

13
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.730
Your mission: find out how a change in one

14
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:43.080
market can move prices in
a completely different one.
